 "context": "<figure id=\"fig-ch22_03_02\"><span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-idp28084320\" data-alt=\"This illustration shows the role of bacteria in the nitrogen cycle. Nitrogen-fixing bacteria in root nodules of legumes convert nitrogen gas, or N2, into organic nitrogen found in plants. Nitrogen-fixing soil bacteria produce ammonium ion, or NH4+. Decomposers, including bacteria and fungi, decompose organic matter, also releasing NH4+. Nitrification is the process by which nitrifying bacteria produce nitrites (NO2-) and nitrates (NO3-). Nitrates are assimilated by plants, then animals, then decomposers. Denitrifying bacteria convert nitrates to nitrogen gas, completing the cycle.\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20241024.164013/resources/feb969f0ae9f4e448b6a88325ce7bfd1a44a6127\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"This illustration shows the role of bacteria in the nitrogen cycle. Nitrogen-fixing bacteria in root nodules of legumes convert nitrogen gas, or N2, into organic nitrogen found in plants. Nitrogen-fixing soil bacteria produce ammonium ion, or NH4+. Decomposers, including bacteria and fungi, decompose organic matter, also releasing NH4+. Nitrification is the process by which nitrifying bacteria produce nitrites (NO2-) and nitrates (NO3-). Nitrates are assimilated by plants, then animals, then decomposers. Denitrifying bacteria convert nitrates to nitrogen gas, completing the cycle.\" width=\"380\" height=\"303\">\n</span>\n\n</figure>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 520246,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Review the processes of the nitrogen cycle pictured, and the role of prokaryotes within those processes. Identify the statement that best describes the process of ammonification in the nitrogen cycle.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1016439,
     "content_html": "Ammonia is released during the decomposition of nitrogen-containing organic compounds."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016440,
     "content_html": "Ammonium is converted to nitrite and nitrate in soils."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016441,
     "content_html": "Nitrate from soil is transformed to gaseous nitrogen compounds."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016442,
     "content_html": "Gaseous nitrogen is fixed to yield ammonia."
    }
   ],
